(add audible objects to scope)
	(bar $Bar)
	(exhaust) {
		*(at $Bar there's $Obj)
		~($Obj has parent #hall)
		(now) ($Obj is #in #hall)
	}

(unlikely [examine (audible $Obj)])
	(bar $Bar)
	~(at $Bar there's $Obj)

(unlikely [listen to ~(audible $)])

(unlikely [listen to (audible $Obj)])
	(bar $Bar)
	~(at $Bar there's $Obj)

(instead of [examine (audible $Obj)])
	(try [listen to $Obj])

(prevent [listen to (audible $Obj)])
	(bar $Bar)
	~(at $Bar there's $Obj)
	You can't hear that at the moment.

(perform [listen to (audible $Obj)])
	(descr $Obj)

(default action (audible $Obj) [listen to $Obj])

%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
%% Orchestra

#orchestra
(singleton *)
(name *)		orchestra
(dict *)
	full ensemble tutti everybody everyone band
	musicians rest instrumentalists members happy amateurs amateur players

(* is #on #stage)

(descr *)

	The Bournebrook Rill Community Orchestra is a kaleidoscopic bunch of
	happy amateurs. The musicians are seated in a large (#seating
	{semi-circle}) around the (#stand).

	(select)
		(par)

		When you moved to the neighbourhood, a complete stranger to
		everyone, you wanted to find a way into the local music life. A
		small sinfonietta happened to be looking for a new conductor,
		and you jumped at the opportunity. The ensemble was in a pretty
		sorry state back then, but with your experience and their
		dedication, things have finally turned around. Your little
		group is now attracting some of the best amateur
		instrumentalists.

		(par)

		The best amateur instrumentalists of Bournebrook Rill, that is.
	(or)
	(stopping)

(prevent [turn to *])
	~(facing audience)
	~(facing sideways)
	You're already facing the orchestra.

(perform [turn to *])
	(face orchestra)

#seating
(plural *)
(singleton *)
(name *)	seating arrangement
(heads *)	seating arrangement semi-circle slice slices
(dict *)

	four first second third fourth slice slices large semi-circle semi
	circle layout plan seated arrangements

(* is #partof #orchestra)
(descr *)

	The seating arrangement is a semi-circle, roughly made up of four
	separate slices.

	(if) (interpreter can embed *) (then)
		(div @picture) (embed resource *)
	(else)
		(par)

		\[ A (link resource 3) {diagram} is included in your (italic)
		(story title) (roman) package. \]

		(par)
	(endif)

	Starting at the far left, you've got the (#violin1) up close, headed by
	the (#concertmaster). Behind them are the two (#harps), and at the back
	you can see the (cymbalist) and the (link [timpani player]) {timpani
	player}.

	(par)

	The second slice begins with the (#violin2). Behind them are the
	(#flutes) and (#piccolo), then the (#clarinets) and (#bassclarinet),
	and at the far back the (#horns).

	(par)

	In the third slice, you've got the (#viola) up front, then the
	(#oboes), the (#enghorn), and the (#bassoons). Back against the wall
	are the (#trumpets), (#trombones), (#basstrombone)
	(if) ~(#basstrombone has parent $) (then)
