#clarinet1
(name *)		first clarinet
(dict *)		agnes clarinette clarinetto
(heads *)		clarinet clarinette clarinetto
(female *)
(musician *)
(* is #partof #clarinets)

(descr *)

			Agnes, first clarinet, has a habit of contorting her
			body like a dancing snake whenever she plays, which can
			be a bit of a distraction, especially when it doesn't
			make sense musically. But when she tries to sit still,
			her phrasing goes all over the place instead, and so
			you'd rather have the writhing.

			(par)

			She is the younger sister of (link [kevin]) Kevin .

#clarinet2
(name *)		second clarinet
(dict *)		mika clarinette clarinetto
(heads *)		clarinet clarinette clarinetto
(male *)
(musician *)
(* is #partof #clarinets)

(descr *)

			Mika, second clarinet, is a blond 35-year-old sales
			clerk at (link [harold]) Harold (no space) 's Garden
			Supplies, who rides a unicycle to work. As good looking
			as ever. Divorced.

			(par)

			An avid runner, Mika was the champion of the annual
			Rill Dash for four years running, until (link [frank])
			Frank robbed him of the title last year.

#bassclarinet
(name *)		bass clarinet
(dict *)		kevin clarinette basso clarinetto
(heads *)		clarinet clarinette
(male *)
(musician *)
(* is #partof #woodwinds)
(slice * 2)

(descr *)

			The bass clarinet, Kevin, is a large, muscular fellow
			with a shaved head, ring in one of his ears, tattooed
			knuckles, and a very kind and humble disposition. He is
			the older brother of (link [agnes]) Agnes .

			(bar $N)
			(if) ($N > 2) ($N < 17) (then)
				(select)
					(par)

					Noticing your glance, he suddenly freezes. Then
					he scrambles to bring his instrument to his
					mouth, and blows a low G. He keeps it up for
					maybe half a bar before withdrawing into
					silence. His cheeks have turned crimson.

					(now) (inhibit clbas-pre-17)
					(bad cue)
				(or)
				(stopping)
			(endif)

