(descr *)
	(if) (did trainwreck) (then)

		Sarah looks at you in disbelief, tears welling up in her eyes.

	(else)

		Sarah, first oboe, is hardly a day over twenty. Tight braids
		arranged in a bun; thin gold-rimmed glasses. She likes to visit
		Chez (link [anna]) Anna , especially on days when (link
		[steve]) Steve is working, and you have fond memories of the
		time when you did Salieri's Concerto for Flute and Oboe with
		her and (link [pia]) Pia as soloists.

		(par)

		She's usually grinning from ear to ear, but right now she looks
		very focused.

	(endif)

