(name *)		first bassoon
(dict *)		david
(heads *)		bassoon
(male *)
(musician *)
(* is #partof #bassoons)

(descr *)

			David, first bassoon, is a short, aubergine-shaped
			fellow with a black mop of hair and a degree in
			cartography.

			(par)

			He usually keeps to himself, although he seems to get
			on well with (link [thomas]) Thomas . And ever since
			October he's been having animated discussions with
			(link [ed]) Ed about some kind of computerized
			adventure stories that they both like.

#bassoon2
(name *)		second bassoon
(dict *)		liu yang
(heads *)		bassoon
(female *)
(musician *)
(* is #partof #bassoons)

(descr *)

			Liu Yang, second bassoon, is a short, energetic lady in
			her thirties.

			(select)

				She used to be in a book club with (link
				[peter]) Peter and (link [joy]) Joy , with
				regular meetings at Chez (link [anna]) Anna.

			(or)
				She is the mother of (link [melody]) Melody .
			(then purely at random)

			(select)
				(par)

				During last year's Halloween concert, she
				demonstrated the Glove Trick: You put a rubber
				glove over the top of the bassoon, and push it
				all the way inside. Then, you play a creepy
				melody that goes all the way down to the low
				B-flat. At that point, all holes are covered,
				and a rubber hand will slowly rise out of the
				instrument.

			(or)
			(stopping)

